# ${{APP_NAME}}

A website and JSON API on PHP's built-in web server, created with Code on the Go.

## Run

Tap **Run app**, then open <http://localhost:${{PORT}}> in a browser on this device. Tap
**Cancel Run app** to stop the server. From the terminal:

```bash
php -S localhost:${{PORT}} -t public
```

## Routes

| Method | Path                  | Response                        |
| ------ | --------------------- | ------------------------------- |
| GET    | `/`                   | an HTML page                    |
| GET    | `/api/hello?name=Ada` | `{"message":"Hello, Ada!"}`     |
|        | `/style.css`          | the stylesheet, served as a file |
|        | anything else         | `404` with a JSON error         |

## Test

Tap **Run tests**. `tests/AppTest.php` calls the request handler directly, so the tests need no
server and no network connection.

## Project structure

```
${{APP_NAME}}/
  composer.json         # name and the start script
  public/index.php      # front controller: every request that is not a file lands here
  public/style.css      # a static file, served as is
  src/App.php           # routes
  tests/AppTest.php     # tests
```
